# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Finder writes .DS_Store into every directory it displays, recording view
# settings (icon positions, window size, sort order). Harmless locally, but it
# also embeds the directory listing — including names of since-deleted files —
# which is why it is treated as an information disclosure finding when it ends
# up on a web server.
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linux
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.bak
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Completed checklists are audit evidence and may name findings in a live
# estate. Keep filled-in copies out of the repo unless that is deliberate.
*-completed.md
*-filled.md
/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only if someone builds the script rather than `go run`-ing it.
/compliance-report
/audit-run

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
audit-run.log
*.cis.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# State records the audit identity and every binding it created. It is the
# teardown record and must not be committed.
#
# .terraform/ holds downloaded provider binaries — the google provider alone is
# ~116 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Never commit it.
#
# terraform.tfvars IS committed: it holds an organization ID, a project ID and
# a list of auditor emails. None of those are credentials, and committing it
# means anyone can reproduce exactly what was applied.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log

# .terraform.lock.hcl SHOULD be committed — it pins provider versions so every
# operator resolves the same ones. It is small and contains no secrets.
!**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — NEVER delete these, in any repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The audit runs by impersonation precisely so that no service account key
# exists. Committing one would break safeguard 5.2, which this kit measures.
*.json.key
*-key.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results and settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# >>> DELETE THIS WHOLE BLOCK IN A CUSTOMER ENGAGEMENT REPOSITORY >>>
#
# There, results are the deliverable and belong in git, and the settings are
# shared by the whole audit team so that everyone scores against identical
# criteria. See "Running with a team" in docs/cis-ig1-audit-runbook.md.
#
# Here, they are ignored. This repository is public and holds the kit's own
# development. Audit output names real projects, buckets and IAM principals,
# and a live IAM inventory has reached this history twice already — both times
# from `git add -A` sweeping a directory nobody meant to commit.
/audit-state/
/config/*
!/config/readme.md
!/config/*.example
#
# <<< END OF THE BLOCK TO DELETE <<<
